{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall shut it up.</b> For then the spreading will be recognizable — for a person who sees a thing every day and it grows little by little does not perceive its growth. And so Noah waited seven days in the mission of the dove in order to perceive the diminishing of the waters. And one cannot say here that he should make a mark around the lesion and thereby perceive the spreading — for perhaps the afflicted person will erase the mark and make another one farther away, so that it will appear not to have spread, and the priest will declare him pure. But in the case of a netek he does make a mark from the hair, as it writes והתגלח — because that is a mark that cannot be falsified." "<b>And deep.</b> It is found in Torat Kohanim that ועמוק אין מראה מן העור is stated to reveal the meaning of the verse above — lest you say: since it is written above עמוק מן העור, therefore it is impure, but if the lesion is level with the flesh, no — therefore ועמוק אין מראה is stated: even if it is not deep, if it is level with the flesh and appears deep, it causes impurity and requires isolation. And likewise one may explain regarding שחין, where it is written initially והנה אין מראה שפל מן העור etc. and וטמאו הכהן, and after it is written ושפלה איננה מן העור — which implies that it causes impurity and requires isolation. And thus one may resolve all the verses in this section. But according to Rashi, that עמוק means 'its appearance is like the sun, deeper than the shade' — this is not so compelling. Nevertheless, one can find a case in a very ruddy person who is exceedingly white, and then the appearance of the lesion is not deep relative to the skin, because the skin is whiter than the lesion. From R. Meiram, who heard from his father R. Ya'akov HaLevi z\"l. And at first glance this is forced, for the Sages said: בהרת עזה כשלג — if so, how can one find a person whiter than snow?"], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:07.045294621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}